"echo.info.title" = "What is an Echo";
"echo.info.what.title" = "What it is";
"echo.info.what.body" = "Echo is a shared experience around a location-tagged moment. It combines multiple perspectives of the same instant into one visual thread and only opens once at least 2 participants accept.";
"echo.info.how.title" = "How it works";
"echo.info.how.body" = "Echo detects moments from mutuals in the same area (up to 500 m) and time window (24 h). Once active, you can navigate between perspectives (bottom bar) and moments (up/down).";
"echo.info.privacy.title" = "Privacy";
"echo.info.privacy.body" = "Echo is created between mutuals, but it keeps who could view it at that time. If the relationship changes later, it remains visible; it only blurs when the moment audience (best friends or custom list) does not include you. Inside Echo, you see your moments and moments from participants who accepted.";
"echo.info.status.title" = "States";
"echo.info.status.body" = "Active means the Echo is still open and other people can still join during its 24-hour window. Expired means that window has ended and the Echo closes, so no one else can join.";
"echo.info.controls.title" = "Controls";
"echo.info.controls.body" = "Swipe up/down to change moments, use the bottom bar to switch perspectives, and the menu to leave the Echo. You cannot leave while the Echo is active: leaving unlocks when its 24 h window ends. If you leave, your moments are removed from that Echo.";

